WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Yeah, it's good to see you.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very happy
to have you here.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to ask you a question,
get right into it.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously you were
critical of the President

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you ran against him
during the primaries in 2016,

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:13.079
said things about how he had an
insatiable desire for attention,

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.316
how there were things about him
that you didn't like.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you feel like
it's been going?

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.055
-There hasn't been a big change.
-No.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.924
It seems very in line with
how we thought it would go.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:29.029
-You know, my job, Seth,
is to talk about the policy

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.733
and always try to stay away from
name calling or personality.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, the country
is frankly more divided today,

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.740 size:81% position:41%
or has settled in --
Hard left, hard right.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.109 size:75% position:38%
Neither side listens
to the other side.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
So all we're focusing on now
is the middle,

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.681 size:88% position:44%
those people who are not
hard right or hard left.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'll tell you
who else I focus on --

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Gen Xers
and the Millennials.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.287
They're the hope for the future
for our country.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
There isn't any question.
They're comfortable

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
with America's role
in the world.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't want
all this conflict.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.761
They don't want name calling.
They just want it to work.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I have a lot of faith
in the Millennials.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.632 line:92%
I think they are the future,

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:09.402
and they are committed
to improving our country.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.904 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Do you feel like --

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.405 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's community up.
Here's the other thing, see,

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're all focused
on the President, okay.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.244 line:92%
What's the president doing?

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.314
I mean, really, does the
President affect you every day?

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.784
What affects you every day
are your neighbors, your job.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.019 line:92%
Right? Those are the things --

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't stress how much
he affects my job every day.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. For you.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-For guys in your business...

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.259
-I'm an outlier. I'm an outlier.
-Yeah, you're right.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm an outlier.
-But don't you think coming

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.163
from New Hampshire like you did
with the town halls

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.899 size:84% position:42%
and the way it works,
it should be bottom up.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-So everybody in this audience

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
needs to make --
you think this is politics.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:45.505 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's not. Okay?

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody here
needs to do something

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
to bring some improvement
where they live.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:52.912
Don't wait for the big boss
or the President or anybody.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do it.
Because if we don't do that,

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.183
we lose the essence of what
our country's all about.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:57.951 line:92%
-That's a very good point.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.587 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think that is a --

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.857 size:81% position:41%
what about, you know,
obviously there was --

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:07.393
it was a big field that ran
against Donald Trump in 2016.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of the people
were critical of him

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:10.763 size:81% position:41% line:92%
the same way you were.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they have since
joined his cabinet.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have since returned
to the Senate

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the House and support him
and his legislation.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.671
If you were in a position,
obviously, as a governor,

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.474
you have to deal with him less,
but if you were in the House,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you were in the Senate
right now,

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
how would you approach
being a Republican

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.478
dealing with Donald Trump?
-Well, I think, you know,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:29.582
Seth, I've been a sort of
an iconoclast all of my career.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.084 line:92%
See, look, when I got in,

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:34.721
my job was not to report to the
Republican National Committee.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't think it should,
to be a Democrat,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
to report to the
Democratic National Committee.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.392 line:92%
You happen to be a Republican

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're for
less government,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.895 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you're a Democrat for X.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
But at the end,
I have to do a job.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I have to look myself
in the mirror.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.903
And it doesn't matter to me what
the partisans want me to do.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:54.374
And, so, you know, my focus
every day is economic growth,

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
jobs, but there's
another thing.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:58.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't just have prosperity
touching people at the top.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.380 line:92%
Everybody has to feel it.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
So in our state,
we expanded Medicaid.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:03.616 line:92%
I want healthcare for people.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
You imagine if you didn't have
any healthcare,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.619 line:92%
what your life would be like?

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want our people
in the minority community

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
to feel as though
they got a shot.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sick of politics,
aren't you?

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.894 line:92%
I mean, I'm sick of politics!

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
So let's --
what I try to do is

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:21.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
let's look at a problem
and go and fix it,

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.835 line:92%
and that's all you can do.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I served for a long time
in Washington,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.272 line:92%
18 years as a congressman.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:31.110
Sometimes I worked against my
own President and my own party.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:31.911 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay? So what?

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.347
If I have --
I fought to balance the budget.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:37.684
I had to fight at times the
first President Bush on that.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what? I mean,
there were a lot of reforms.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we reformed welfare
for poor people,

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.923
I said,
"Well, we should reform welfare

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
for rich people
in corporations."

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.160 size:75% position:38% line:92%
What's fair is fair.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if you operate
with a compass,

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
you operate
with a set of values,

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.299 line:92%
the jobs are not that hard.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.468 line:92%
And when you get heat, so what?

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.537 line:92%
So, for me, think about this,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had the convention
in Ohio, okay?

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't go.
It was in my own state.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-People were, like, outraged.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-I didn't endorse him.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I wrote in John McCain --

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
my hero, John McCain.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A great guy.
And, so, at the end,

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.820 size:75% position:38%
people, today, still
are angry with me.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this wasn't
because I was upset

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
because something happened
to me.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was not the values
I believed in.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last point -- I wrote
a book called "Two Paths."

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.430
You know, look, we have a lot
of trouble in this country.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can either look at people
who are struggling

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can --
you can make excuses,

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:33.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can demagogue them
and make them more negative,

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
or you can look at them
and say,

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Look, you got problems,
I agree.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.145 line:92%
Let's go fix them together."

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's a difference
between negative populism

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
and positive populism.
I want to give people hope.

